{"name":"Newburyport","hex":"#445a79","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Newburyport","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A coastal city in Essex County, Massachusetts, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Newburyport"}],"entries":[{"title":"Newburyport, Massachusetts","blocks":[{"text":"Newburyport is a coastal city in Essex County, Massachusetts, United States, 35 miles (56 km) northeast of Boston. The population was 18,289 at the 2020 census. A historic seaport with a vibrant tourism industry, Newburyport includes part of Plum Island. The mooring, winter storage, and maintenance of recreational boats, motor and sail, still generate much of the city's income. A Coast Guard station oversees boating activity, especially in the sometimes dangerous tidal currents of the Merrimack River."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Newburyport%2C_Massachusetts.jpg/330px-Newburyport%2C_Massachusetts.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Newburyport%2C_Massachusetts","wikidata":"Q54134"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Seal_of_Newburyport%2C_Massachusetts.png/120px-Seal_of_Newburyport%2C_Massachusetts.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/16/Seal_of_Newburyport%2C_Massachusetts.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Seal_of_Newburyport%2C_Massachusetts.png/120px-Seal_of_Newburyport%2C_Massachusetts.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASeal_of_Newburyport%2C_Massachusetts.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Custom_House_Maritime_Museum.jpg/5